          "kind": "native",
          "stratum": "core",
          "text": "Harbor Bikes owner's manual. The hydraulic brake system works by pushing fluid through a sealed line when the lever is pulled. Bleed the brakes whenever the lever feels soft."
        },
        {
          "kind": "native",
          "stratum": "core",
          "text": "Clean and lubricate the chain every 300 kilometres. The drive train wears faster in winter."
        },
        {
          "kind": "native",
          "stratum": "core",
          "text": "Store the bicycle indoors. Salt water corrosion is not covered by the warranty."
        }
      ]
